<header><p class="st-kicker">other · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Voivodeship of Serbia and Banat of Temeschwar</h1><p class="st-meta">1849 CE – 1860 CE · capital Temeschwar</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Austrian crown land created after the 1848 revolution in southern Hungary, nominally Serbian but run by imperial officials from Temeschwar.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After the defeat of the Hungarian revolution, Emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/franz-joseph-i">Franz Joseph</a> rewarded the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> who had fought for the dynasty in the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/serbian-vojvodina">Serbian Vojvodina</a> by creating, in November 1849, a separate crown land from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/backa">Bačka</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/banat">Banat</a> and parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Srem</a>. He took the title of Grand Voivode himself and placed the government at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeschwar</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The voivodeship was run by German-speaking officials under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna's</a> neo-absolutist system, with a military governor and no elected assembly. Its borders were drawn to include large Romanian, German and Hungarian populations, so <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a> were only a minority, and Serb leaders were disappointed. Roads, railways and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> trade developed, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/timisoara">Temeschwar</a> grew as an industrial centre.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>As <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vienna">Vienna</a> sought compromise with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hungary">Hungary</a>, the crown land was abolished in 1860 and most of its territory returned to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kingdom-of-hungary-1526-1867">Kingdom of Hungary</a> (1526-1867), with parts of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syrmia">Srem</a> going to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/slavonia">Slavonia</a>. The name survived in the modern Serbian province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vojvodina">Vojvodina</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/voivodeship-of-serbia-and-banat-of-temeschwar.jpg" alt="Voivodeship of Serbia and Banat of Temeschwar" width="320" height="205"><figcaption>Image: Jembezmamy · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Serbian_Vojvodina.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1849 CE – 1860 CE</dd><dt>Century</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>other</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>bureaucratic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Temeschwar</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Franz Joseph I</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Orthodox and Catholic Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>German, Serbian, Romanian, Hungarian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Serbian Voivodeship, Vojvodina of Serbia and Tamiš Banat</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=voivodeship-of-serbia-and-banat-of-temeschwar" aria-label="Voivodeship of Serbia and Banat of Temeschwar on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5183 565 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Voivodeship of Serbia and Banat of Temeschwar lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M5503 821L5474 838M5503 821L5381 747M5503 821L5398 749"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5474 838h0M5381 747h0M5398 749h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5503 821h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5503 821h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks its capital. <a href="/atlas?year=1854&amp;focus=voivodeship-of-serbia-and-banat-of-temeschwar">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
